libs/ex36_mesh is derived from MFEM example 36 (examples/ex36.cpp).
The comparison base is upstream commit 8452c8cc7f (git describe: v4.9-5-g8452c8cc7f).
At that commit, the MFEM library sources are unchanged: the diff does not touch
fem/, linalg/, mesh/, or the other library directories.

The build-relevant local difference is:

1. Root CMakeLists.txt gains `set(MFEM_ENABLE_EXAMPLES ON)` before the examples target.
2. examples/CMakeLists.txt gains `add_subdirectory(ex36_mesh)`.
3. The new directory examples/ex36_mesh. Those sources are the files in libs/ex36_mesh,
   excluding this NOTICE text and the patch file below.

libs/ex36_mesh/upstream-mfem-8452c8cc7f.patch contains items 1 and 2.
Apply it from a clean MFEM tree at 8452c8cc7f, and copy libs/ex36_mesh to
examples/ex36_mesh. A local .gitignore addition of `.cache` and
`compile_commands.json` is not required to build the example and is not in the patch.

The copied example sources keep the MFEM example-36 header comment that was
present in the local example. They do not replace the MFEM BSD-3-Clause license.

Configure the example with FILE_IO_SOURCE_DIR set to the libs/file_io directory
of this repository. libs/ex36_mesh/cmake/find_file_io.cmake adds that directory
with add_subdirectory. It does not fetch file_io from a private remote.

